# Test requests for the Galactic Slicer API (Visual Studio, Rider or the VS Code REST Client).
# Start the API first (dotnet run), then send the requests one by one.
# 1. Register and log in, 2. copy the "token" from the login response into @token below.

@GalacticSlicer.Api_HostAddress = http://localhost:5190
@token = paste-the-token-from-the-login-response-here

### Register a player
POST {{GalacticSlicer.Api_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "pilot@galacticslicer.local",
  "password": "User123!"
}

### Log in (returns the JWT)
POST {{GalacticSlicer.Api_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "pilot@galacticslicer.local",
  "password": "User123!"
}

### Planets (public)
GET {{GalacticSlicer.Api_HostAddress}}/api/planets
Accept: application/json

### Characters in the Shop (public)
GET {{GalacticSlicer.Api_HostAddress}}/api/characters
Accept: application/json

### The logged-in player's progress
GET {{GalacticSlicer.Api_HostAddress}}/api/progress/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Start the Tatooine mission: 10 random questions without the answers
GET {{GalacticSlicer.Api_HostAddress}}/api/missions/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Search the player's own challenges
GET {{GalacticSlicer.Api_HostAddress}}/api/challenges/search?searchString=firewall&subject=Network%20Security
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Practice: 10 random questions from one subject
GET {{GalacticSlicer.Api_HostAddress}}/api/practice/questions?subject=Linux%20Command%20Line
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Buy a character (409 when the player has too few Credits)
POST {{GalacticSlicer.Api_HostAddress}}/api/characters/2/buy
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Admin only: create a planet (401 without a token, 403 for a normal player)
POST {{GalacticSlicer.Api_HostAddress}}/api/planets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Dagobah",
  "order": 7,
  "cssClass": "dagobah",
  "subject": "Network Security",
  "description": "A swamp planet for testing."
}
